### Violations. The original mft.ttl models these as subclasses of
### mft:Violation, a kind of Value; the BFO refactor models them as processes,
### so these are historical annotations rather than logical class mappings.
<https://fandaws.com/ontology/bfo/valuenet-moral-foundations#HarmProcess> vn-core:historicallyCorrespondsTo <https://w3id.org/spice/SON/HaidtValues#Harm> .
<https://fandaws.com/ontology/bfo/valuenet-moral-foundations#CheatingProcess> vn-core:historicallyCorrespondsTo <https://w3id.org/spice/SON/HaidtValues#Cheating> .
<https://fandaws.com/ontology/bfo/valuenet-moral-foundations#BetrayalProcess> vn-core:historicallyCorrespondsTo <https://w3id.org/spice/SON/HaidtValues#Betrayal> .
<https://fandaws.com/ontology/bfo/valuenet-moral-foundations#SubversionProcess> vn-core:historicallyCorrespondsTo <https://w3id.org/spice/SON/HaidtValues#Subversion> .
<https://fandaws.com/ontology/bfo/valuenet-moral-foundations#DegradationProcess> vn-core:historicallyCorrespondsTo <https://w3id.org/spice/SON/HaidtValues#Degradation> .
<https://fandaws.com/ontology/bfo/valuenet-moral-foundations#OppressionProcess> vn-core:historicallyCorrespondsTo <https://w3id.org/spice/SON/HaidtValues#Oppression> .
<https://fandaws.com/ontology/bfo/valuenet-core#ValueViolationProcess> vn-core:historicallyCorrespondsTo <https://w3id.org/spice/SON/HaidtValues#Violation> .
### Folk corpus correspondences (D-014). Each corpus value here evokes, indicates or
### operationalizes the class without naming it, so it is recorded as a related match and
### never as a label. The trigger lexicons attached to these IRIs reach the class through
### this assertion. folk:Accomplishment is the IRI its trigger lexicon uses; folk.ttl
### declares the value as FolkValues.owl#:Accomplishment.
<https://fandaws.com/ontology/bfo/valuenet-folk#AdventureDisposition> vn-core:hasRelatedConceptualMatch <http://www.ontologydesignpatterns.org/ont/values/FolkValues.owl#Daring> .
